# corelab — the list of secrets. This file is a description only; it holds no values.
# The source files live on the workstation in ~/.config/corelab/secrets
# (scripts/gen-secrets.sh), never in the repo.
#
# name                     | consumer             | format                                          | placeholder
# db_root_password         | mariadb              | one line                                        | <DB_ROOT_PASSWORD>
# db_wordpress_password    | mariadb + wordpress  | one line                                        | <DB_WORDPRESS_PASSWORD>
# wordpress_admin_password | wpcli (first run only) | one line                                      | <WP_ADMIN_PASSWORD>
# grafana_admin_password   | grafana              | one line                                        | <GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD>
# relay_credentials        | postfix              | texthash line: [relay.corelab.test]:587 USER:PASS | [relay.corelab.test]:587 <USER>:<PASSWORD>
# relay_ca_cert            | postfix              | PEM (ext-01's relay.crt; public, but lab-specific) | <RELAY_CA_PEM>
#
# On the VM (done by scripts/push-secrets.sh):
#   - directory: /var/lib/corelab/secrets, owner root, mode 0700
#   - files: owner root, mode 0444 (the containers run with different UIDs;
#     the 0700 parent directory means only root can reach them on the host)
#   - SELinux label: container_file_t (chcon -R -t container_file_t)
#   - the .ready marker file is put in place LAST; without it corelab-stack does not start
